Today is Thursday evening.
My badminton game finished.
I played with Amit, Neha, and Sanjay today.
Now I go to the club counter.
A man is sitting there.
I put my rented racket on the counter.
"Dada," I say.
He looks at me and asks, "Tell me, Madam."
"I took this racket at half past five," I say.
"Okay, Madam," Dada says.
He writes something in his notebook.
"I gave the money earlier," I say.
"Yes, I remember," he says with a smile.
I thank him.
I turn and go back toward the court.
My friends Amit, Neha, and Sanjay are waiting for me there.
Amit asks me, "Maya, shall we go?"
"Yes, let's go," I say.
We all come out of the club together.
